@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "The Starfold";
}

<div class="desktop-layout">
    <div class="profile-section">
        <div class="profile-image-container">
            <img src="/images/profile-default.png" alt="Profile Image" class="profile-image profile-default">
            <img src="/images/profile-press.png" alt="Profile Image Pressed" class="profile-image profile-press">
        </div>
    </div>

    <section class="bio">
    <h1>Hey Hey Hey, Imago Dei!</h1>
    <p>The name's Renai Paragonic, Celestial Shepherd for the Kingdom of God. I'm a relatively new Christian PNGTuber with a focus on
    topics a little past the "basics of Christianity". My goal is for all of my content to be grounded in scripture and ultimately point folks ever more in
    the direction of Christ. Along the way, I'll likely be playing some games, writing some stories, and spending time getting to know anyone who wants 
    to get to know me. Whether you're Christian or not Christian yet, welcome to the Starfold! Together, let's light it up! <a href="https://youtu.be/gIRDMPudmLg">Here's what I'm all about!</a></p>
    
    <div class="social-container">
        <img src="/images/Talmy.png" alt="Talmy" class="talmy-image talmy-left">
        <div class="social-links">
            <a href="https://twitch.tv/renaiparagonic"  aria-label="Twitch"><i class="fab fa-twitch fa-lg"></i></a>
            <a href="https://youtube.com/@@renaiparagonic"  aria-label="YouTube"><i class="fab fa-youtube fa-lg"></i></a>
            <a href="https://x.com/paragonicray"  aria-label="X (formerly Twitter)"><i class="fab fa-x-twitter fa-lg"></i></a>
        </div>
        <img src="/images/Talmy.png" alt="Talmy" class="talmy-image talmy-right">
    </div>

    <div class="accordion">
        <div class="accordion-item">
            <button class="accordion-header">
                <span>What's Your Deal?</span>
                <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="accordion-content">
                <p>Ah, a discerning viewer who is after more than my paragraph-long cutesy blurb. You'd like a peek behind the beloved Comedian's Mask which I have named Renai Paragonic. In short, I am a man who grew up on and with the Internet. Sure - my sense of humor was irreparably molded by meme culture, but I've always truly seen the Internet as a modern miracle. The possibilities out here are endless. Renai was born from a desire to walk <a href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew%2014%3A22-33&version=NASB1995">atop the digital sea for Christ.</a> Slipping my mask back on: <strong>these waters can get pretty choppy and dark.</strong> As a Nomad of the Stars, part of my calling <a href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew%205%3A14-16&version=NASB1995">is to help light it up.</a> </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="accordion-item">
            <button class="accordion-header">
                <span>What Type of Content Do You Make?</span>
                <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="accordion-content">
                <p>I'm unsure, at the moment. That's the neat part! I'm very down to make <em>whatever</em>, as long as <em>whatever</em> meets two immutable requirements:</p>
                <ol>
                    <li>I need to be able to find a way to <a href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Romans%2012%3A1&version=NASB1995">glorify God or otherwise point to Christ with it.</a></li>
                    <li>It's gotta interest me in some way. This does include things that are so bad or wild that they become entertaining.</li>
                </ol>
                <p>See what I've been up to at my <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@@RenaiParagonic">YouTube channel.</a> My coming streams will likely lead with a presentation or Bible Study before switching to games (Pokémon, predominantly). Other ideas in development!</p>

            </div>
        </div>

          <div class="accordion-item">
            <button class="accordion-header">
                <span>Where'd You Get Your PNGTuber?</span>
                <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="accordion-content">
                <p>My artist is the illustrious <a href="https://youtube.com/@@phrogpollen">PhrogPollen</a>. If you like my design or the design of my dear sheep Talmy (you do), you should absolutely <a href="https://noexcusesphrog.wixsite.com/phrogsoddsandends">pop over to her shop</a> or <a href="https://vgen.co/PhrogPollen/commissions">hit her up on VGen</a>. Get yourself some art before the demand for her work catches up with her insane creative skill. I can also vouch that her commission process was hassle-free and exceeded my expectations a great deal.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="accordion-item">
            <button class="accordion-header">
                <span>What Are Your Creds?</span>
                <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="accordion-content">
                <p>If Christ said to jump, I'd ask "How high?" If Christ said to sprint, I'd ask "How far?" If Christ told me to <a href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew%2028%3A19-20&version=NASB1995">go and make disciples of all nations</a>, I wouldn't have any questions because the statement is abundantly clear. I am an amateur theologian and Christian educator with my church's high school ministry. I've dug a good deal into logical arguments for God as well as Western Philosophy as a whole. <strong>The important bit:</strong> I always intend the heart of all of my teaching to be scripture. If you are a Christian and <em>ever</em> feel as though I am misrepresenting scripture, reach out to me. I would love to talk it out. On or off record. Ooh, new content idea! </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
</div>
